+        "foreignOnly": "An incentive whose own terms pay it only to a production from abroad (or a co-production with a foreign partner) is held so where a primary source of its figure says it (tools/person/markets-producer/readings.json names the words): Azerbaijan, Colombia, Estonia, Greenland, Latvia, Montenegro, Mongolia, Panama, the Philippines and Taiwan. The production company is the life's own, in the country of its first citizenship, so a film it makes there isn't foreign and is refused the incentive (told, producing.abroad); one it makes in another country is foreign there. The game makes no co-production, so an incentive open to co-productions isn't paid at home either. A territory's incentive counts a production from its sovereign's country as foreign (the game's reading: a Dane's film in Greenland is foreign there). Read on 2026-11-04; until then no limit was read and every such incentive was paid at home too.",
